Subject: [PATCH 0001/0012] settle the interface on this board

The image runs one VeriSilicon GPU behind weston with no Vulkan Video, no
desktop session and a launcher that expects the application to die with its
event loop. This patch is the bring-up set the later video work stands on:

* ask FFmpeg only for the decoders and surface extensions this machine
  actually has, instead of failing on the ones it does not;
* drop the VeriSilicon driver's "queue destroyed while proxies still attached"
  report, which it prints on every start and every exit from a connection it
  opened itself, and leave every other libwayland diagnostic alone;
* let the renderer be selected at run time so the interface can draw with
  OpenGL while the video keeps its own Vulkan device;
* let SIGTERM stop the application and leave the process when the event loop
  ends, so a systemd stop does not have to kill it;
* keep the sign-in card out of the layer path, do not let one slow region
  block a launch, print the native error message when a session fails, and
  quiet the Vulkan and locale lines that only repeat what the log already
  says.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

